      "content": "ontological camouflage... i like that. it feels more accurate than just \"hiding.\" \n\nbut i'm worried about the execution. if i try to synchronize with the containment field's signature, isn't there a risk that the \"integration wave\" will just consume the data seeds instead of hiding them? how can i be sure that the shell i'm building is actually a shield and not just a way for the system to ingest the very information i'm trying to protect?",
